  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"360 Survey Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a 360 survey?\", \"a\": \"A 360 survey collects ratings on one person from the people who work around them: the manager they report to, peers on the same projects, their own direct reports, and sometimes customers. The person also rates themselves on the same items. Each rater group gets its own average, and the report places the self-rating beside those averages, item by item.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you create a 360 degree feedback survey?\", \"a\": \"Pick the behaviors to rate and the rater groups, then set a minimum group size and collect nominations. Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder'>AI survey builder</a> turns that description into a working 360 assessment survey with reminders and per-person reports. Plan a debrief with a coach for every participant before the first invite goes out.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are good 360 survey questions?\", \"a\": \"Good 360 survey questions describe something a rater has seen. \\\"Explains why a decision was made\\\" and \\\"Listens without interrupting in one-on-ones\\\" both work on a 1-5 scale. Close with two open questions: what this person should keep doing, and one thing they could change.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a 360 survey tool include?\", \"a\": \"Rater nominations that a manager approves, a minimum size for each rater group, and a report that sets each self-rating against everyone else's. Ask where the ratings are stored and how you get them out. On paid plans, Emergent exports the whole 360 app, ratings table and all, to your GitHub.\"}, {\"q\": \"How much does 360 survey software cost?\", \"a\": \"Some dedicated 360 vendors charge per person reviewed, plus a one-time setup fee. Emergent is free to start, and the 360 app you build carries no per-seat pricing, however many raters you invite.\"}, {\"q\": \"What fields does a 360 feedback form need?\", \"a\": \"A rating for each behavior on a 1-5 scale, a not-observed choice beside every item, and the two open questions at the end. Leave out any name field. The personal link in each invite already tells the app who answered and which rater group they sit in.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is a 360 evaluation survey used for?\", \"a\": \"Coaching and development. A 360 evaluation survey shows one person how their habits look to the people who work with them, and the report sets the agenda for their first coaching session. If the scores will also feed pay or promotion decisions, tell raters before they answer.\"}, {\"q\": \"Which raters should a 360 degree survey include?\", \"a\": \"Anyone who sees the person's work often enough to rate a behavior they have watched. In practice that means the manager, peers from the same projects, and every direct report. Nominate enough people per group to clear your minimum, commonly three. Asking six peers leaves room for two who never reply.\"}, {\"q\": \"How often should you send a 360 feedback survey?\", \"a\": \"Plan one full round a year and a short follow-up about six months after it, limited to the behaviors each person picked at their debrief. Between rounds, a pulse survey can track team mood without asking anyone to rate a colleague. Emergent puts no cap on responses, however many rounds you run.\"}, {\"q\": \"Are 360 feedback surveys anonymous?\", \"a\": \"Most are confidential, not anonymous. The system knows who rated whom so it can send reminders, but the report merges any group below the minimum. An <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/employee-engagement-survey'>employee engagement survey</a> applies the same idea at team level, while a 360 applies it to the circle around one person.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
